# Figma ↔ shop UI sync

> **Captured/Updated**: 2026-08-28  
> **Owner**: `@aea-ux-designer`  
> **Traceability**: Issue #274, Design System SOP  

When changing `edge/gateway/ui/` or proposing a **new user journey**, follow
`.cursor/skills/aea-ux-designer/SKILL.md` (Figma section).

- **Runtime source of truth:** `edge/gateway/ui/` CSS/HTML/JS. Do not invent a
  second CSS token system. Figma variables must mirror existing `:root` names.
- **Figma file:** https://www.figma.com/design/4PNLwici0GMwU824BpoZ38
  (`plugin-figma-figma` only; load `/figma-use` before `use_figma`).
- **UI change:** update Figma library + composed frames in the **same MR** (or
  immediately after on the same issue). Refresh `figma/README.md` mappings.
- **New journey:** mockups of screens/states **and** a clickable Figma
  prototype (not disconnected frames). Link the proto URL (file + node) in the
  issue/MR and `figma/README.md`. After the journey ships, sync Figma to match
  the implemented UI.
- **Automated Visual Guard:** Run `python edge/scripts/check_ui_visual_sync.py` to verify wireframe asset integrity (`adaptive-workspace-mvp.svg`/`.png`) and tile element coverage across `edge/gateway/ui/`.
- Do not restyle the live shop in a proposal unless that journey is approved
  to implement. Do not invent BG/US/FR/NFR IDs.
